<title>JAPAN: Japan May copper imports grow 9.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan May copper imports grow 9.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in May totalled 24,753 tonnes, up 9.8 percent from 22,545 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Friday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    May 97	April 97	 May 96</p>
<p> Total	  24,753	  90,582	 22,545</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Zambia	  2,048	   8,518	  3,833</p>
<p> S.Africa	  899	   1,019	    637</p>
<p> Brazil	    707	     200	    nil</p>
<p>Imports in the first five months of calendar 1997 were 187,378 tonnes, up from 170,871 tonnes during the same period last year. Copper imports usually surge in April due to the Generalised System of Preferences (GSP) which allows tariff exemptions for metal imports from designated developing countries.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
